<title>UK: Boots transfers items with BASF unit.</title>
<headline>Boots transfers items with BASF unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Boots Co Plc said it had agreed to bring forward transfer of products with Knoll AG, the pharmaceuticals arm of BASF AG of Germany.</p>
<p>Knoll will pay the British pharmaceuticals company 10 million marks in the deal.</p>
<p>Boots, which sold Boots Pharmaceuticals to BASF a year ago, said it would regain control of over-the-counter medicine sales in India, Pakistan and Canada, while Knoll will take control of global and local prescription products in Australia, New Zealand and South Africa.</p>
<p>Boots sold its pharmaceuticals business for 840 million stg.</p>
<p>Boots said the deal on Monday &quot;completes the transfer of both product portfolios ahead of schedule.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44171 542 7717</p>
